m variables ${X}_{i}$ as follows:\n\n$$\n{X}_{i}=\\{\\begin{aligned}1,\\,i\\text{th member of the sample has the characteristic} \\\\ 0,\\,\\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, provided that $N≫n,$ the random variables ${X}_{i}$ can be considered independent and identically distributed. Under this assumption, we have\n\n$$\n{X}_{i}∼\\text{Bernoulli}(p)\\,1\\le i\\le n\n$$\n\nwhere $p$ is the proportion of the population that has the characteristic.\n\nTherefore, the random variable $X,$ defined as \n\n$$\nX={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{X}_{i}\n$$\n\ncan be approximated as a binomial random variable $X≈B(n,p),$ where\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[X]=np,\\,\\text{Var}[X]=np(1-p).\n$$\n\nIn our case, we're told that the population size is significantly larger than the sample size. Moreover, we have \n\n$$\np=55%=0.55,\\,n=20.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\nX≈B(20,0.55)\n$$\n\nand we have the following results for the mean and variance:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[X] & =np \\\\  & =20\\cdot 0.55 \\\\  & =11 \\\\ \\text{Var}[X] & =np(1-p) \\\\  & =20\\cdot 0.55\\cdot (1-0.55) \\\\  & =4.95\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186159800 :answer-field/correct "answer-75de330a-021b-5e46-ada2-d963d4b8b6d2" :answer-field/choices ["answer-c9f5f4b6-b070-593f-8481-3aeaeb2a2dad" "answer-c9dc5707-7d2f-56a8-ab1f-d8df8930478d" "answer-75de330a-021b-5e46-ada2-d963d4b8b6d2" "answer-396108d7-e165-5e51-a218-82c7a7387856" "answer-d17050cc-7332-556c-9082-471225f91b2c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c9f5f4b6-b070-593f-8481-3aeaeb2a2dad" :answer/id #uuid "c9f5f4b6-b070-593f-8481-3aeaeb2a2dad" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\text{E}[X]=11,\\,\\text{Var}[X]=3.95" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c9dc5707-7d2f-56a8-ab1f-d8df8930478d" :answer/id #uuid "c9dc5707-7d2f-56a8-ab1f-d8df8930478d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\text{E}[X]=11,\\,\\text{Var}[X]=4.25" :db/ensu