the population that has the characteristic.\n\nTherefore, the random variable $X,$ defined as \n\n$$\nX={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{X}_{i}\n$$\n\ncan be approximated as a binomial random variable $X≈B(n,p),$ where\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[X]=np,\\,\\text{Var}[X]=np(1-p).\n$$\n\nIn our case, we're told that the population size is significantly larger than the sample size. Moreover, we have \n\n$$\np=20%=0.2,\\,n=45.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\nX≈B(45,0.2)\n$$\n\nand we have the following results for the mean and variance:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[X] & =np \\\\  & =45\\cdot 0.2 \\\\  & =9 \\\\ \\text{Var}[X] & =np(1-p) \\\\  & =45\\cdot 0.2\\cdot (1-0.2) \\\\  & =7.2\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-c458ea31-a563-52a9-afec-c274ae8a1c99"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-c458ea31-a563-52a9-afec-c274ae8a1c99" :answer-field/id #uuid "c458ea31-a563-52a9-afec-c274ae8a1c99" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-c25585ea-c83f-57ce-bd51-f45fd169466f" :answer-field/choices ["answer-99c04746-0912-59fe-8ac3-72bf6d45cc6f" "answer-b3857716-e886-53a6-a471-de30e220e0b6" "answer-d6f6b528-5571-544d-9a05-17fb2cca69c6" "answer-c25585ea-c83f-57ce-bd51-f45fd169466f" "answer-6722c3cd-ec7f-5097-b55f-d96f54ca6df5"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-99c04746-0912-59fe-8ac3-72bf6d45cc6f" :answer/id #uuid "99c04746-0912-59fe-8ac3-72bf6d45cc6f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\text{E}[X]=10,\\,\\text{Var}[X]=7.2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b3857716-e886-53a6-a471-de30e220e0b6" :answer/id #uuid "b3857716-e886-53a6-a471-de30e220e0b6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\text{E}[X]=10,\\,\\text{Var}[X]=8.1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d6f6b528-5571-544d-9a05-17fb2cca69c6" :answer/id #uuid "d6f6b528-5571-544d-9a05-17fb2cca69c6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\text{E}[X]=9,\\,\\text{Var}[X]=6.5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c25585ea-c83f-57ce-bd51-f45fd169466f" :answer/id #uuid "c25585ea-c83f-57ce-bd51-f45fd169466f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\text{E}[X]=9,\\,\\text{Var}[X]=7.2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6722c3cd-ec7f-5097-b55f-d96f54ca6df5" :answer/id #uuid "6722c3cd-ec7f-5097-b55f-d96f54ca6df5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\text{E}[X]=9,\\,\\text{Var}[X]=8.1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-669ea571-4e73-5129-bf0b-c10dd97639ff" :question/id #uuid "669ea571-4e73-5129-bf0b-c10dd97639ff" :question/math-academy-id "q-146407" :question/problem "Suppose we have a random sample of size $n=400$ from a population where $32%$ of the population has a particular characteristic. Let the random variable ${X}_{i}$ be equal to\n\n$$\n{X}_{i}=\\{\\begin{aligned}1,\\,i\\text{th member of the sample has the characteristic} \\\\ 0,\\,\\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $i=1,…,400.$ If the statistic $X$ is defined as\n\n$$\nX={\\sum }_{i=1}^{400}{X}_{i}\n$$\n\nfind approximate values of $\\text{E}[X]$ and $\\text{Var}[X].$\n\n*Hint: You may assume that the population size is significantly larger than the sample size.*" :question/worked-solution "Suppose we have a random sample of size $n$ from a population of size $N,$ and we define the sequence of random variables ${X}_{i}$ as follows:\n\n$$\n{X}_{i}=\\{\\begin{aligned}1,\\,i\\text{th member of the sample has the characteristic} \\\\ 0,\\,\\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, provided that $N≫n,$ the random variables ${X}_{i}$ can be considered independent and identically distributed. Under this assumption, we have\n\n$$\n{X}_{i}∼\\text{Bernoulli}(p)\\,1\\le i\\le n\n$$\n\nwhere $p$ is the proportion of the population that has the characteristic.\n\nTherefore, the random variable $X,$ defined as \n\n$$\nX={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{X}_{i}\n$$\n\ncan be approximated as a binomial random variable $X≈B(n,p),$ where\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[X]=np,\\,\\text{Var}[X]=np(1-p).\n$$\n\nIn our case, we're told that the population size is significantly larger than the sample size. Moreover, we have \n\n$$\np=32%=0.32,\\,n=400.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\nX≈B(400,0.32)\n$$\n\nand we have the following results for the mean and variance:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[X] & =np \\\\  & =400\\cdot 0.32 \\\\  & =128 \\\\ \\text{Var}[X] & =np(1-p) \\\\  & =400\\cdot 0.32\\cdot (1-0.32) \\\\  & =87.04\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-011c0d7f-8d89-5535-a87a-f90d68f3ba54"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-011c0d7f-8d89-5535-a87a-f90d68f3ba54" :answer-field/id #uuid "011c0d7f-8d89-5535-a87a-f90d68f3ba54" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-3e6f11e6-66eb-560f-8f48-f16a3c3e83e3" :answer-field/choices ["answer-e4a8b4bf-bfb7-56ab-86ea-c7c08d289e7c" "answer-7f65d500-2aeb-54b4-8dd1-a097b21dfc81" "answer-6846d9c1-083e-5354-8dbe-53b3e9a399b8" "answer-3e6f11e6-66eb-560f-8f48-f16a3c3e83e3" "answer-0cda9d0b-c153-562d-ac1d-798cf69026f8"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e4a8b4bf-bfb7-56ab-86ea-c7c08d289e7c" :answer/id #uuid "e4a8b4bf-bfb7-56ab-86ea-c7c08d289e7c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\text{E}[X]=121,\\,\\text{Var}[X]=75.66" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7f65d500-2aeb-54b4-8dd1-a097b21dfc81" :answer/id #uuid "7f65d500-2aeb-54b4-8dd1-a097b21dfc81" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\text{E}[X]=121,\\,\\text{Var}[X]=81.33" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6846d9c1-083e-5354-8dbe-53b3e9a399b8" :answer/id #uuid "6846d9c1-083e-5354-8dbe-53b3e9a399b8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\text{E}[X]=128,\\,\\text{Var}[X]=81.27" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3e6f11e6-66eb-560f-8f48-f16a3c3e83e3" :answer/id #uuid "3e6f11e6-66eb-560f-8f48-f16a3c3e83e3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\text{E}[X]=128,\\,\\text{Var}[X]=87.04" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0cda9d0b-c153-562d-ac1d-798cf69026f8" :answer/id #uuid "0cda9d0b-c153-562d-ac1d-798cf69026f8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\text{E}[X]=128,\\,\\text{Var}[X]=93.56" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186162431 :question/problem "Suppose that $45%$ of the voting population plans to vote for candidate $A$ in the upcoming mayoral election. A random sample of size $n=20$ is taken from the population and asked about their voting preference. \n\nWhat is the mean and variance of $\\overset{^}{\\,p},$ the proportion of voters in the sample that plan to vote for candidate $A?$ Round your answers to $4$ decimal places where appropriate.\n\n*Hint: You may assume that the population size is significantly larger than the sample size.*" :question/worked-solution "Suppose we have a random sample of size $n$ from a population of size $N,$ and we define the sequence of random variables ${X}_{i}$ as follows:\n\n$$\n{X}_{i}=\\{\\begin{aligned}1,\\,i\\text{th member of the sample has the characteristic}, \\\\ 0,\\,\\text{otherwise}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, provided that $N≫n,$ we have that\n\n$$\nX={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{X}_{i}≈B(n,p)\n$$\n\nwhere $p$ is the proportion of the population that have the characteristic, and \n\n$$\n\\text{E}[X]=np,\\,\\text{Var}[X]=np(1-p).\n$$\n\nThe sample proportion $\\overset{^}{\\,p}$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\overset{^}{\\,p}=\\overset{―}{X}=\\frac{X}{n}.\n$$\n\nUsing the properties of expectation and variance, it is straightforward to show that\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[\\overset{^}{\\,p}]=p,\\,\\text{Var}[\\overset{^}{\\,p}]=\\frac{p(1-p)}{n}.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have $p=45%=0.45,$ and $n=20.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[\\overset{^}{\\,p}] & =45%=0.45, \\\\ \\text{Var}[\\overset{^}{\\,p}] & =\\frac{0.45(1-0.45)}{20} \\\\  & ≈0.0124\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to $4$ decimal places." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186159788 :answer-field/correct "answer-174dc03d-1058-5222-a2c8-328de8d3dfb9" :answer-field/choices ["answer-174dc03d-1058-5222-a2c8-328de8d3dfb9" "answer-0896db64-9d17-550f-8644-691706316afb" "answer-2ea9fa72-6c20-5814-8a9d-b2946f694c67" "answer-ba7e5957-681c-5abe-8f63-81da11f56105" "answer-3ee15f42-cfc1-5622-b98b-eb798bf29abd"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-174dc03d-1058-5222-a2c8-328de8d3dfb9" :answer/id #uuid "174dc03d-1058-5222-a2c8-328de8d3dfb9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\text{E}[\\overset{^}{\\,p}]=0.45,\\,\\text{Var}[\\overset{^}{\\,p}]=0.0124" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0896db64-9d17-550f-8644-691706316afb" :answer/id #uuid "0896db64-9d17-550f-8644-691706316afb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\text{E}[\\overset{^}{\\,p}]=0.45,\\,\\text{Var}[\\overset{^}{\\,p}]=0.0175" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2ea9fa72-6c20-5814-8a9d-b2946f694c67" :answer/id #uuid "2ea9fa72-6c20-5814-8a9d-b2946f694c67" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\text{E}[\\overset{^}{\\,p}]=0.45,\\,\\text{Var}[\\overset{^}{\\,p}]=0.0231" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ba7e5957-681c-5abe-8f63-81da11f56105" :answer/id #uuid "ba7e5957-681c-5abe-8f63-81da11f56105" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\text{E}[\\overset{^}{\\,p}]=0.55,\\,\\text{Var}[\\overset{^}{\\,p}]=0.0124" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3ee15f42-cfc1-5622-b98b-eb798bf29abd" :answer/id #uuid "3ee15f42-cfc1-5622-b98b-eb798bf29abd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\text{E}[\\overset{^}{\\,p}]=0.55,\\,\\text{Var}[\\overset{^}{\\,p}]=0.0231" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-1d5c4439-72cc-5a29-8805-27f9db8f5589" :question/id #uuid "1d5c4439-72cc-5a29-8805-27f9db8f5589" :question/math-academy-id "q-146450" :question/problem "Suppose that  $8%$ of a particular university's student population attends the law school. A random sample of $n=100$ students is taken from the population and asked which school they attend.\n\nWhat is the mean and variance of $\\overset{^}{\\,p},$ the proportion of students in the sample who attend the law school? Round your answers to $4$ decimal places where appropriate.\n\n*Hint: You may assume that the population size is significantly larger than the sample size.*" :question/worked-solution "Suppose we have a random sample of size $n$ from a population of size $N,$ and we define the sequence of random variables ${X}_{i}$ as follows:\n\n$$\n{X}_{i}=\\{\\begin{aligned}1,\\,i\\text{th member of the sample has the characteristic}, \\\\ 0,\\,\\text{otherwise}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, provided that $N≫n,$ we have that\n\n$$\nX={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{X}_{i}≈B(n,p)\n$$\n\nwhere $p$ is the proportion of the population that have the characteristic, and \n\n$$\n\\text{E}[X]=np,\\,\\text{Var}[X]=np(1-p).\n$$\n\nThe sample proportion $\\overset{^}{\\,p}$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\overset{^}{\\,p}=\\overset{―}{X}=\\frac{X}{n}.\n$$\n\nUsing the properties of expectation and variance, it is straightforward to show that\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[\\overset{^}{\\,p}]=p,\\,\\text{Var}[\\overset{^}{\\,p}]=\\frac{p(1-p)}{n}.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have $p=8%=0.08,$ and $n=100.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[\\overset{^}{\\,p}] & =8%=0.08, \\\\ \\text{Var}[\\overset{^}{\\,p}] & =\\frac{0.08(1-0.08)}{100} \\\\  & ≈0.0007\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to $4$ decimal places." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-e48890ff-d63d-57c7-b77b-86bd5ac0b261"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-e48890ff-d63d-57c7-b77b-86bd5ac0b261" :answer-field/id #uuid "e48890ff-d63d-57c7-b77b-86bd5ac0b261" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-0f582a26-8981-5aeb-8c9a-798c57cf7fa6" :