an and variance of $\\overset{^}{\\,p},$ the proportion of teenagers in the sample who like science fiction novels? Round your answers to $4$ decimal places where appropriate.\n\n*Hint: You may assume that the population size is significantly larger than the sample size.*" :question/worked-solution "Suppose we have a random sample of size $n$ from a population of size $N,$ and we define the sequence of random variables ${X}_{i}$ as follows:\n\n$$\n{X}_{i}=\\{\\begin{aligned}1,\\,i\\text{th member of the sample has the characteristic}, \\\\ 0,\\,\\text{otherwise}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, provided that $N≫n,$ we have that\n\n$$\nX={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{X}_{i}≈B(n,p)\n$$\n\nwhere $p$ is the proportion of the population that have the characteristic, and \n\n$$\n\\text{E}[X]=np,\\,\\text{Var}[X]=np(1-p).\n$$\n\nThe sample proportion $\\overset{^}{\\,p}$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\overset{^}{\\,p}=\\overset{―}{X}=\\frac{X}{n}.\n$$\n\nUsing the properties of expectation and variance, it is straightforward to show that\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[\\overset{^}{\\,p}]=p,\\,\\text{Var}[\\overset{^}{\\,p}]=\\frac{p(1-p)}{n}.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have $p=22%=0.22,$ and $n=25.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[\\overset{^}{\\,p}] & =22%=0.22, \\\\ \\text{Var}[\\overset{^}{\\,p}] & =\\frac{0.22(1-0.22)}{25} \\\\  & ≈0.0069\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to $4$ decimal places." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-1e53a0ea-2177-529a-b607-5f54cb66e41c"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-1e53a0ea-2177-529a-b607-5f54cb66e41c" :answer-field/id #uuid "1e53a0ea-2177-529a-b607-5f54cb66e41c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-ec57b051-ab02-5e79-99b8-56f8c9fadb67" :answer-field/choices ["answer-ec57b051-ab02-5e79-99b8-56f8c9fadb67" "answer-4fecbd1a-4f33-567e-8978-268629ae9bcd" "answer-83135bc2-29fc-5570-8ca1-f6392afa94d1" "answer-1ed2ddc3-b4dc-59ae-9d8b-031