arger than the number in the sample.*" :question/worked-solution "Suppose we have a random sample of size $n$ from a population of size $N,$ and we define the sequence of random variables ${X}_{i}$ as follows:\n\n$$\n{X}_{i}=\\{\\begin{aligned}1,\\,i\\text{th member of the sample has the characteristic}, \\\\ 0,\\,\\text{otherwise}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, provided that $N≫n,$ we have that\n\n$$\nX={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{X}_{i}≈B(n,p)\n$$\n\nwhere $p$ is the proportion of the population that have the characteristic, and \n\n$$\n\\text{E}[X]=np,\\,\\text{Var}[X]=np(1-p).\n$$\n\nThe sample proportion $\\overset{^}{\\,p}$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\overset{^}{\\,p}=\\overset{―}{X}=\\frac{X}{n}.\n$$\n\nUsing the properties of expectation and variance, it is straightforward to show that\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[\\overset{^}{\\,p}]=p,\\,\\text{Var}[\\overset{^}{\\,p}]=\\frac{p(1-p)}{n}.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have $p=10%=0.1,$ and $n=20.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[\\overset{^}{\\,p}] & =10%=0.1, \\\\ \\text{Var}[\\overset{^}{\\,p}] & =\\frac{0.1(1-0.1)}{20} \\\\  & =0.0045.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-b14feaef-0c14-5d3c-a394-226d0415b9de"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-b14feaef-0c14-5d3c-a394-226d0415b9de" :answer-field/id #uuid "b14feaef-0c14-5d3c-a394-226d0415b9de" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-fbbe8668-1cdb-5f50-82eb-12abca7abfdb" :answer-field/choices ["answer-fbbe8668-1cdb-5f50-82eb-12abca7abfdb" "answer-29c329a0-2b65-5553-80ed-a63f5cbd64ad" "answer-b32e31b8-7ee2-5888-8fe2-b6582e214786" "answer-8bfe0081-89a0-5f3a-8044-d6903a1aec34" "answer-e86497ec-cf36-5810-9fc4-eb1d50286589"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-fbbe8668-1cdb-5f50-82eb-12abca7abfdb" :answer/id #uuid "fbbe8668-1cdb-5f50-82eb-12abca7abfdb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\text{E}[\\overset{^}{\\,p}]=0.1,\\,\\text{Var}[\\overset{^}{\\,p}]=0.0045" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-29c329a0-2b65-5553-80ed-a63f5cbd64ad" :answer/id #uuid "29c329a0-2b65-5553-80ed-a63f5cbd64ad" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\text{E}[\\overset{^}{\\,p}]=0.1,\\,\\text{Var}[\\overset{^}{\\,p}]=0.0064" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b32e31b8-7ee2-5888-8fe2-b6582e214786" :answer/id #uuid "b32e31b8-7ee2-5888-8fe2-b6582e214786" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\text{E}[\\overset{^}{\\,p}]=0.1,\\,\\text{Var}[\\overset{^}{\\,p}]=0.0081" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8bfe0081-89a0-5f3a-8044-d6903a1aec34" :answer/id #uuid "8bfe0081-89a0-5f3a-8044-d6903a1aec34" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\text{E}[\\overset{^}{\\,p}]=0.9,\\,\\text{Var}[\\overset{^}{\\,p}]=0.0045" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e86497ec-cf36-5810-9fc4-eb1d50286589" :answer/id #uuid "e86497ec-cf36-5810-9fc4-eb1d50286589" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\text{E}[\\overset{^}{\\,p}]=0.9,\\,\\text{Var}[\\overset{^}{\\,p}]=0.0081" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-2e62b0fb-05ae-5348-8fa8-26e1b9d8b974" :question/id #uuid "2e62b0fb-05ae-5348-8fa8-26e1b9d8b974" :question/math-academy-id "q-146441" :question/problem "A bag contains a large number of equally-sized buttons, of which $15%$ are white. A random sample of $n=18$ buttons is taken from the bag.\n\nWhat is the mean and variance of $\\overset{^}{\\,p},$ the proportion of white buttons in the sample? Round your answers to $3$ decimal places where appropriate.\n\n*Hint: You may assume that the number of buttons in the bag is significantly larger than the number in the sample.*" :question/worked-solution "Suppose we have a random sample of size $n$ from a population of size $N,$ and we define the sequence of random variables ${X}_{i}$ as follows:\n\n$$\n{X}_{i}=\\{\\begin{aligned}1,\\,i\\text{th member of the sample has the characteristic}, \\\\ 0,\\,\\text{otherwise}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, provided that $N≫n,$ we have that\n\n$$\nX={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{X}_{i}≈B(n,p)\n$$\n\nwhere $p$ is the proportion of the population that have the characteristic, and \n\n$$\n\\text{E}[X]=np,\\,\\text{Var}[X]=np(1-p).\n$$\n\nThe sample proportion $\\overset{^}{\\,p}$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\overset{^}{\\,p}=\\overset{―}{X}=\\frac{X}{n}.\n$$\n\nUsing the properties of expectation and variance, it is straightforward to show that\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[\\overset{^}{\\,p}]=p,\\,\\text{Var}[\\overset{^}{\\,p}]=\\frac{p(1-p)}{n}.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have $p=15%=0.15,$ and $n=18.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[\\overset{^}{\\,p}] & =15%=0.15, \\\\ \\text{Var}[\\overset{^}{\\,p}] & =\\frac{0.15(1-0.15)}{18} \\\\  & ≈0.007\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to $3$ decimal places." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-3ae3297d-2ab7-525a-83e9-568931f0c244"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-3ae3297d-2ab7-525a-83e9-568931f0c244" :answer-field/id #uuid "3ae3297d-2ab7-525a-83e9-568931f0c244" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-de1a4b59-e152-53b9-b98f-578e556fb269" :answer-field/choices ["answer-9073635c-c291-5d2a-89b8-35dca7c94744" "answer-de1a4b59-e152-53b9-b98f-578e556fb269" "answer-afbdf9af-161b-565e-b86c-9d06f52deaa7" "answer-59127361-a7c6-54be-8be7-6e1bedd5c145" "answer-e4313ddb-7ae8-58f9-81a8-402669642b8b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9073635c-c291-5d2a-89b8-35dca7c94744" :answer/id #uuid "9073635c-c291-5d2a-89b8-35dca7c94744" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\text{E}[\\overset{^}{\\,p}]=0.15,\\,\\text{Var}[\\overset{^}{\\,p}]=0.005" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-de1a4b59-e152-53b9-b98f-578e556fb269" :answer/id #uuid "de1a4b59-e152-53b9-b98f-578e556fb269" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\text{E}[\\overset{^}{